{"t": 186.72, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "parallel_sshi_fbr_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed due to insufficient output voltage under heavy loads (S4-S6) and excessive voltage under light loads (S3). I am implementing a Parallel Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) circuit. By adding an LC-tank (L1 and S1) in parallel with the piezo, we can invert the voltage on the piezo capacitance Cp at its extrema, significantly increasing the energy extracted per cycle. A full-bridge rectifier (FBR) is used to channel this energy to the storage capacitor, and a Zener diode (DZ33) is added to the output to clamp the voltage at 3.3V, ensuring v_max <= 3.6V for S3. A larger storage capacitor (4.7uF) is used to minimize ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "parallel_sshi_fbr_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed due to insufficient output voltage under heavy loads (S4-S6) and excessive voltage under light loads (S3). I am implementing a Parallel Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) circuit. By adding an LC-tank (L1 and S1) in parallel with the piezo, we can invert the voltage on the piezo capacitance Cp at its extrema, significantly increasing the energy extracted per cycle. A full-bridge rectifier (FBR) is used to channel this energy to the storage capacitor, and a Zener diode (DZ33) is added to the output to clamp the voltage at 3.3V, ensuring v_max <= 3.6V for S3. A larger storage capacitor (4.7uF) is used to minimize ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "